"So what did the Spanish leave? Excavations on Heping Island began in 2011, and a Taiwan–Spain team dug again from 2016 and widened the dig in 2019. They have uncovered the foundations of a church, Todos los Santos, and its cemetery. One person was buried with hands folded in prayer. Early findings suggest some of the people came from Europe, others from Asia, and possibly some from Africa. The site, which also holds much older layers, is now a national archaeological site.": "8c22ffec87fe",
